---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { doctor, site } from '../data/site.js';
---

<Page
  title="For doctors — training and workshops"
  description="Hands-on facial aesthetics workshops for practising doctors, run by Dr Hitesh Aggarwal, MBBS DDVL."
  slug="for-doctors"
  intro="Hands-on training in facial aesthetics for practising doctors, plus referrals and case discussion."
  showByline={true}
>
  <p>
    Alongside clinical practice, {doctor.name} teaches — a thread that goes back to his training
    years, where he taught medical students and internees in the dermatology department at J.J.M.
    Medical College, Davangere.
  </p>

  <h2>Facial aesthetics workshops</h2>

  <p>
    A hands-on workshop for practising doctors covering facial anatomy, injectable technique,
    patient selection, and — the part most short courses skip — recognising and managing
    complications.
  </p>

  <p>
    The emphasis is on doing fewer things properly rather than demonstrating a long menu.
    Anatomy and patient selection take up more of the day than product technique, because that is
    where avoidable harm actually comes from.
  </p>

  <h3>Typically covered</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Relevant facial anatomy, with the danger zones treated as the core of the session</li>
    <li>Assessment and patient selection — including who should be declined</li>
    <li>Injectable technique, practised under supervision</li>
    <li>Recognising vascular compromise early, and what to do in the first minutes</li>
    <li>Consent, documentation and realistic expectation-setting with patients</li>
  </ul>

  <div class="note">
    <h3>Details to be confirmed</h3>
    <p>
      Upcoming dates, venue, fee and group size are not listed here yet. Write to
      <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> with your qualification and current
      practice, and you will be sent details of the next session.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>Referrals</h2>

  <p>
    Referrals from colleagues are welcome, particularly for diagnostically difficult cases —
    rashes that have not responded as expected, hair loss where the pattern is unclear, and
    genital dermatoses, which are often where a general practice reaches the limit of what it can
    reasonably assess.
  </p>

  <p>
    Please send the history, what has already been tried and for how long, and any photographs or
    reports. A written summary of the assessment goes back to the referring doctor.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a><br />
    {doctor.name}, {doctor.qualifications}<br />
    {doctor.registration}
  </p>
</Page>
